# OS Auditing Configuration file

# Records execution attempts made by 64-bit and 32-bit programs when the originating login user has an audit UID of 1000 or higher:
#   -a always,exit: Always create an audit event when a matching system call finishes.
#   -F arch=b64: Apply the rule to the 64-bit/32-bit syscall ABI.
#   -S execve,execveat: Watch the two system calls used to execute programs.
#   -F auid>=1000: Include sessions originally logged in as users with audit UID 1000 or higher.
#   -F auid!=unset: Exclude processes that have no established login identity, normally system daemons.
#   -k spe_cli: Tag matching events with the searchable key spe_cli.
-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S execve,execveat -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k spe_cli
-a always,exit -F arch=b32 -S execve,execveat -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=unset -k spe_cli
